This product is a Cangjie (仓颉) X.509 certificate module for the EU Digital
Identity Wallet on HarmonyOS. It wraps the platform X.509 capability
(stdx.crypto.x509) behind a stable facade and adds CRL (RFC 5280) parsing /
revocation checking and certificate extension utilities that the platform
library does not provide.

The interface surface is driven by the consumer usage of the EU Digital
Identity Wallet ISO 18013-5 security library for Swift:

    eudi-lib-ios-iso18013-security
    Copyright (c) European Commission
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
    https://github.com/eu-digital-identity-wallet/eudi-lib-ios-iso18013-security

(That Swift library uses apple/swift-certificates + swift-asn1 for X.509;
this Cangjie module replaces them with stdx.crypto.x509 + a hand-written
RFC 5280 CRL/DER layer for the gaps.)

This product depends on and/or bundles the following third-party software:

  - cangjie-stdx 1.1.3.1 (Apache License 2.0) — Cangjie extended standard
    library; stdx.crypto.x509 backs certificate parsing and chain validation.
    Bundled under entry/libs/stdx/.

  - OpenSSL runtime libraries (libcrypto_openssl.z.so, libssl_openssl.z.so)
    and libsecurec.so, bundled under entry/libs/arm64-v8a/ for on-device
    execution of stdx.crypto.x509 (loaded via dlopen at runtime).

